MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Standing in the Breach feels like a natural follow-up to You Should Be So Lucky because reflective songwriting is what I most want to hear next.",
    "The bluesy rock of Exile On Main Street and the roots connections of Dylan, Cash, and the Nashville Cats connect with my interest in Clapton and Hendrix, even though neither is my choice today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "A live Beatles recording and broad greatest-hits collections do not match my current interest in a studio album whose songs feel connected.",
    "Neil Diamond's polished pop, Blackstar's experimental direction, and Corazon's Latin pop emphasis move away from the roots and blues sound I want right now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Recognizing a familiar rock artist is not enough to make me want every recording, remaster, or compilation associated with them.",
    "My interest in Blown Away makes country worth considering, but it does not mean outlaw country will feel equally appealing."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent interest in You Should Be So Lucky makes reflective songwriting a stronger reason to choose an album today than a broad connection to classic rock.",
    "I need a specific reason to try something: an appealing guitar style or songwriting connection matters more than a familiar name, and a remaster offers less reason to explore."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You picked up my interest in roots and guitar-based music, but familiar artists alone matter less to me today than reflective songwriting and a compelling studio album."
}
